 "explanation": "Tempester n°55: eight more Quantize values for real-time recording: dotted 8th, 16th and 32nd, 64th, 64th triplet, 8th and 16th quintuplets, 16th septuplets (Main 1.5.0.2). Forum request n°15, Docs/analyses/feature-copy-divisions.md. Before: Quantize (global [address], Shift + soft knob 3) is 4th, 8th, 8T, 16th, 16T, 32nd, 32T or Off (0-7); the index reads 26 tables and jump tables ([address] / [address] grids, [routine]...), is saved in the project and checked against 7 at load ([routine]): it cannot grow. After: eight more values, « 8 Dot » (72 ticks at 96 ppq), « 16 Dot » (36), « 32 Dot » (18), « 64th » (6), « 64T » (4), « 8 Quint » (5 per half note), « 16 Quint » (5 per quarter note), « 16 Sept » (7 per quarter note), and the knob walks all 16 from the longest to the shortest (author's order B, 12/11/2026): 1/4, 8 Dot, 1/8, 8 Quint, 16 Dot, 1/8T, 1/16, 16 Quint, 32 Dot, 1/16T, 16 Sept, 1/32, 1/32T, 64th, 64T, Off (QEDIT, tables POSITION_OF / VALUE_AT); DSI's values keep their codes 0-7. A fine value is kept apart (FINE, RAM [address], 1-8; 0 at power-on) and the global stays at 7 = Off: every DSI reader of the Quantize (the step grids, 16 Time Steps, Beat Events, roll and arp grids, the Loop screen, the project file) sees Off, a path the factory OS already runs. Only real-time recording uses the fine grid: FINEREC, entered by the tail jump of [routine] into [routine], rounds the note's tick to the nearest grid point first (ties down, the next point through [routine] as [routine] does for DSI's grids); the Off path of [routine] then stores the exact tick (step = tick / 8 rounded, Time Shift = the remainder, -3..+4) and playback ([routine]) gives it back exactly. Quintuplets and septuplets are rounded to the tick (96 ppq): 0, 19, 38, 58, 77 for 16 Quint. Grids start at the beat's tick 0 (a dotted grid runs across bar lines, as in a sequencer's dotted grid). The knob label shows « Quant: 8 Dot »... ([routine] case 6, QLBL). Saved with the project (author, 12/11/2026): the project parameter record (44 words, version 5) keeps Off (7) in word 4 and gets FINE in word 18 as 0x5100 | FINE (SAVEHOOK); words 18-33 are written from RAM and skipped by every loader, so the factory OS and earlier Tempester versions ignore it and load Off. LOADHOOK sets FINE from word 18 when its high byte is 0x51, the value 1-8 and word 4 says Off; otherwise FINE = 0 (a project without it loads plain). After power-on Quantize Off is plain Off; a DSI value on the knob clears FINE. Not made: dotted LFO rates (the Voice OS computes the LFO frequency, rom:001706: Main-only round); fine grids for step entry, 16 Time Steps, roll and arp (their code assumes 8-tick steps and the 8-entry tables). Context: main loop (UI knob, pad or MIDI note in record). FINEREC: 3 divisions and 1-2 per loop pass by constants of its own table (never 0), no teq; stack 0x30 bytes. Free flash 0x9D079C80-0x9D079FDF.",
